 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508448,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Graph the linear inequality: <span data-math=\"y\\, > \\,\\frac{2x}{3} - 1\">y\\, &gt; \\,\\frac{2x}{3} - 1</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBbU1NIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--39c2bf9c055793268aa7ce3f221b603b6512acd4/CS_Figure_05_05_024.jpg\" alt=\"A dashed line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 2.5. The line passes through the following points, (negative 10, negative 7.5), (0, negative 1), (5, 2.5), and (7.5, 3.75). The region above the line is shaded. Note: all values are approximate.\">"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Graph the line <span data-math=\"y = \\frac{2}{3}x - 1\"></span> with a dotted line since the inequality is strictly greater than.</p>\n<p>Shade above the line since this is “<i>y</i> &gt;”.</p>\n<p>Test <span data-math=\"(0,0)\"></span> to be sure shading above the line is correct.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 > \\frac{2}{3}\\left( 0 \\right) - 1\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 > -1\"></span> is true, so <span data-math=\"(0,0)\"></span> is in the solution. The shading should include <span data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span>. The shading is correct.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
